 "title": "Glass Pad",
 "category": "Pads and atmospheres",
 "text": "Sound: a soft, glassy, shimmering pad: the bell-like digital pads of the mid-80s, fading in rather than striking.\n\nHow it's built: FM. A sine modulator two octaves up shakes the carrier sine gently (LIN FM, low), which adds a glassy shimmer without the clang; a slow attack, a long release; Chorus and a large Reverb. Six voices.\n\nPlay: slow chords high on the keyboard.\n\nTweak: the carrier's LIN FM (more glass), the modulator's TUNE, the envelope's ATTACK.",
